---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import roadmap from '../data/roadmap.json';
import entries from '../data/entries.json';
import entities from '../data/entities.json';
import artwork from '../data/artwork.json';
---
<Site title="About Demonology" description="The Christian mission, research standards and future direction of Demonology.">
<section class="wrap archive methodology"><p class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE</p><h1>About Demonology</h1><p class="lead">Exploring the darkness through the light of Scripture.</p><p>Demonology is a Christian research archive grounded in Biblical, Trinitarian theology. We affirm Jesus Christ as Lord and God and study spiritual evil in light of his authority.</p><p>The archive distinguishes explicit Biblical teaching from historical testimony, theological interpretation and extra-Biblical tradition. Its purpose is education and research, not the promotion of occult practices.</p><h2>Current collection</h2><p>{entries.length} research entries, including {entities.length} entity profiles, and {artwork.length} artworks, including {artwork.filter(a=>a.origin==='Historical artwork').length} historical works. The archive publishes research under owner authorisation, with evidence and confidence recorded individually.</p><p><a href="/research/">Explore research</a> · <a href="/encyclopaedia/">Encyclopaedia</a> · <a href="/media/">Gallery</a> · <a href="/library/">Historical library</a> · <a href="/timeline/">Timeline</a> · <a href="/methodology/">Read our methodology</a></p><h2>The next chapters</h2><p>The milestones below describe delivered capabilities and remaining research priorities, not a list of separately published software versions.</p><h3>Delivered</h3>{roadmap.filter(m=>m.status==='Delivered').map(m=><section class="claim"><p class="status">Delivered · v{m.version}</p><h4>{m.title}</h4><p>{m.description}</p><p class="muted">Continuing: {m.next}</p></section>)}<h3>In development and planned</h3>{roadmap.filter(m=>m.status!=='Delivered').map(m=><section class="claim"><p class="status">{m.status} · v{m.version}</p><h4>{m.title}</h4><p>{m.description}</p><p class="muted">Next: {m.next}</p></section>)}<p><a href="/corrections/">Corrections and contributions</a></p></section>
</Site>
